A command's answer follows the switch that plays its clip.

A switch kept no command of its own until its clip showed. A command whose
clip another switch replaced while it loaded was never answered, and its
caller waited out its whole wait to hear timeout; it is now answered
cancelled (superseded) at once. A command for the clip the chain was already
loading was answered playing before the clip showed, and when the clip
showed the switch, which carried no command, answered the command cancelled
although the clip then played to its end. The command now takes the loading
switch over and is answered as that clip goes: playing once it shows, ended
at its end. A command the switch carried before is cut short by the newer
one, as when another switch takes over.

